  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Inside, the scenery can be like a drawing, with treasure materials and primeval essence often dozens of times denser than the outside world. A dying blessed land can still host inheritances built inside it, and that decay can end in the land vanishing.",
      "chapters": [
        325
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "How a mortal aperture becomes an immortal one is covered on immortal ascension. The mortal aperture itself is on aperture and primeval essence.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_ascension",
        "sys_aperture_and_primeval_essence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every blessed land faces an earthly calamity every ten years and a heavenly tribulation every hundred years. A land spirit can prolong a blessed land that is near the end of its lifespan; without one, outsiders can enter and plunder, and exhaustion of immortal essence can finish the collapse.",
      "chapters": [
        374
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "decay-and-tribulations",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal apertures of rank six and rank seven Gu Immortals are blessed lands; apertures of rank eight and rank nine Gu Immortals are grotto-heavens.",
      "chapters": [
        609
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "names-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_aperture",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_gu_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ordinary personal blessed lands belong to one Gu Immortal, and when cultivation reaches rank eight that immortal aperture becomes a grotto-heaven.",
      "chapters": [
        795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "names-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Blessed lands are also graded by size and foundation. Small, medium, and high grades differ in area, in how large a tributary of the river of time they draw, in how many immortal essence beads they form, and in whether leftover heaven and earth qi can refine a mortal Gu into an Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        609
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "names-by-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Some famous blessed lands are not one Gu Immortal’s private aperture. Super forces cut off portions of their own blessed lands and piece those portions into a shared camp, including Snowy Mountain blessed land among demonic path forces. Personal immortal apertures remain private storage and living space; damage to them is treated as a severe loss.",
      "chapters": [
        795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shared-camps",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_super_force",
        "loc_snowy_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Many factors can matter in a siege: whether the land is whole, whether a land spirit remains, immortal essence stocks, desolate beast guards, Immortal Gu, immortal killer moves, Immortal Gu Houses, and Gu Immortals defending it. Fang Yuan states the overall measure as the quantity of dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        820
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defense",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dao marks are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defense",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
